# Rule 5/5 (composite engine). A workflow that BOTH pins a mutable action tag
# AND declares no permissions block is a doubly-weak CI setup: a moved tag could
# run malicious code with an over-broad default token. Either leaf alone warns;
# together it is an escalation. The leaves (KEUR-CICD-001/003) still fire on
# their own — this composite only combines their evidence.
#
# Reference composite: the "both together is worse" logic is DATA here, not C++.
# @see docs/adr/ADR-009-composite-rules-and-facts.md
# @implements ADR-009.composite
id: KEUR-CICD-010
maturity: 2
title: High-risk CI workflow (mutable action tag AND no permissions block)
category: sast
severity: error
engine: composite
action: block
composite:
  all: KEUR-CICD-001 KEUR-CICD-003
message: "High-risk workflow: it pins a mutable action tag AND has no permissions block. A re-pointed tag could run malicious code with an over-broad default token. Pin actions to a SHA and add a least-privilege permissions: block."
fix: "Pin all actions to commit SHAs and add a scoped permissions: block — fixing either leaf clears this composite."
